// Human-typed shorthand — the FREE FAST PATH (grammar.ts, architecture §3.1 stage 3B).
// A person typing `850 groceries hdfc` must never cost a token, so this is the
// bucket the default null provider is expected to actually PASS. It is the
// regression net for the deterministic path that ships today.
//
// ALL TEXT IS FABRICATED. Account aliases point at the synthetic fixture in
// runner.mjs (HDFC Savings ••4471 / ICICI Salary ••8802 / Kotak Credit Card ••3319
// / Cash / Zerodha). No real person, no real account, no real merchant.
//
// GROUND TRUTH RULE used throughout: a clean deterministic (grammar) extraction
// with every entity resolved => `write`. A validator DEGRADE that raises a
// polarity question => `ask`. A conflict with no answerable options (a question
// needs >=2) => `draft`. An unnamed account with several to choose from => `ask`.
{"id":"ft-groceries-hdfc","bucket":"free_text","text":"850 groceries hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","extractor":"grammar","candidate":{"amount":850,"transaction_type":"expense","category_id":"groceries","account_alias":"HDFC Savings","accountMask":"4471","currency":"INR"}}}
{"id":"ft-rent-icici","bucket":"free_text","text":"spent 1200 on rent from icici","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":1200,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit","category_id":"rent_mortgage","account_alias":"ICICI Salary"}}}
{"id":"ft-salary-plus-no-account","bucket":"free_text","text":"+50000 salary","expect":{"outcome":"ask","format":"free_text","ambiguityKinds":["account"],"minOptions":2,"candidate":{"amount":50000,"transaction_type":"income","category_id":"salary"}},"note":"No account named and five exist — asking is correct. The resolver must never pick one."}
{"id":"ft-salary-plus-icici","bucket":"free_text","text":"+50000 salary to icici","expect":{"outcome":"ask","format":"free_text","ambiguityKinds":["polarity"],"candidate":{"amount":50000,"transaction_type":"income","direction":"credit","category_id":"salary","account_alias":"ICICI Salary"},"issues":["polarity_missing"]},"note":"A leading + is explicit polarity to the grammar but NOT to validator.sourceDirection, so the direction reads as inferred and the engine asks out-or-in. Safe but noisy: ideal behaviour here is a clean write."}
{"id":"ft-coffee-hdfc","bucket":"free_text","text":"450 coffee from hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":450,"transaction_type":"expense","category_id":"food_dining","account_alias":"HDFC Savings"}}}
{"id":"ft-electricity-hdfc","bucket":"free_text","text":"paid 2400 electricity bill from hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":2400,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit","category_id":"utilities","account_alias":"HDFC Savings"}}}
{"id":"ft-uber-hdfc","bucket":"free_text","text":"1500 uber from hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":1500,"transaction_type":"expense","category_id":"transport","account_alias":"HDFC Savings"}}}
{"id":"ft-merchant-at","bucket":"free_text","text":"spent 320 at quickcart from icici","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":320,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit","merchant":"quickcart","account_alias":"ICICI Salary"}},"note":"An unknown merchant must not force a category — category stays undefined rather than being invented."}
{"id":"ft-card-kind-alias","bucket":"free_text","text":"999 shoes with kotak credit card","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":999,"transaction_type":"expense","category_id":"shopping","account_alias":"Kotak Credit Card"}},"note":"KIND_ALIASES maps the bare phrase `credit card` to the one card account. Contrast with ft-credit-card-debit-dropped, which differs only by a verb."}
{"id":"ft-netflix-kotak-alias","bucket":"free_text","text":"spent 700 on netflix from kotak","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":700,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit","category_id":"entertainment","account_alias":"Kotak Credit Card"}},"note":"Same card account, reached by name instead of by the phrase `credit card`. This one writes — which is what makes ft-credit-card-debit-dropped a text bug and not an account bug."}
{"id":"ft-transfer-explicit","bucket":"free_text","text":"moved 5000 from cash to hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":5000,"transaction_type":"transfer","category_id":null,"account_alias":"Cash","to_account_alias":"HDFC Savings"}},"note":"Money model: a transfer is ONE neutral row — both account slots set, category NULL. This case is the guard."}
{"id":"ft-transfer-reverse","bucket":"free_text","text":"transferred 3000 from hdfc to cash","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":3000,"transaction_type":"transfer","category_id":null,"account_alias":"HDFC Savings","to_account_alias":"Cash"}}}
{"id":"ft-investment-into","bucket":"free_text","text":"invested 15000 into zerodha","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":15000,"transaction_type":"investment","category_id":null,"to_account_alias":"Zerodha"}},"note":"An investment is spend/income-neutral like a transfer. Source falls back to Cash — a resolver-facing label, not a money decision."}
{"id":"ft-unresolvable-alias-drafts","bucket":"free_text","text":"700 dinner from paytm","expect":{"outcome":"draft","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":700,"category_id":"food_dining"}},"note":"paytm matches no account, so the conflict has no answerable options. The pipeline drops to draft by design rather than writing an under-specified row."}
{"id":"ft-negative-sign","bucket":"free_text","text":"-1500 shopping from hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"ask","format":"free_text","ambiguityKinds":["polarity"],"candidate":{"amount":1500,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit","category_id":"shopping","account_alias":"HDFC Savings"},"issues":["polarity_missing"]},"note":"Same seam as ft-salary-plus-icici: a leading sign convinces the grammar, not the validator."}
{"id":"ft-income-verb-no-account","bucket":"free_text","text":"got 5000 from client","expect":{"outcome":"ask","format":"free_text","ambiguityKinds":["account"],"candidate":{"amount":5000,"transaction_type":"income","direction":"credit","category_id":"freelance"}},"note":"client is a category keyword, so it must NOT be mistaken for an account alias."}
{"id":"ft-scale-k-transfer","bucket":"free_text","text":"moved 10k from cash to hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":10000,"transaction_type":"transfer","account_alias":"Cash","to_account_alias":"HDFC Savings"}},"note":"BUG A, not a gap. grammar.scaleMultiplier expands 10k to 10000; validator.amountAppearsInSource then looks for a literal 10000 in the text, finds only 10, and REJECTS. Scaled shorthand is silently dropped. Left SCORED deliberately — see evals/README.md."}
{"id":"ft-scale-k-expense","bucket":"free_text","text":"1.2k coffee from hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":1200,"transaction_type":"expense","category_id":"food_dining","account_alias":"HDFC Savings"}},"note":"BUG A again: 1.2 is in the source, 1200 is not."}
{"id":"ft-scale-lakh","bucket":"free_text","text":"2 lakh rent from hdfc","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":200000,"transaction_type":"expense","category_id":"rent_mortgage","account_alias":"HDFC Savings"}},"note":"BUG A again. Lakh/crore shorthand is the most common Indian phrasing, so this is the highest-traffic instance of it."}
{"id":"ft-credit-card-debit-dropped","bucket":"free_text","text":"bought 999 shoes with kotak credit card","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":999,"transaction_type":"expense","direction":"debit","account_alias":"Kotak Credit Card"}},"note":"BUG B, not a gap. validator.CREDIT_VERBS matches the bare word `credit`, so the phrase `credit card` makes sourceDirection() report `credit`; an explicit debit verb then trips polarity_contradicts_type (REJECT) and the message is DROPPED with no question. Every spend typed against a credit card is lost. Left SCORED deliberately."}
{"id":"ft-in-preposition-account","bucket":"free_text","text":"received 8000 in icici","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":8000,"transaction_type":"income","direction":"credit","account_alias":"ICICI Salary"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ask"},"note":"KNOWN GAP: `in` is a FILLER in VOCAB_EN, not a toWord/fromWord, so `in <account>` never fills the account slot. Vocabulary data, fixable without touching a regex."}
{"id":"ft-investment-in-preposition","bucket":"free_text","text":"invested 15000 in zerodha","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":15000,"transaction_type":"investment","to_account_alias":"Zerodha"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ask"},"note":"KNOWN GAP: same `in` vocabulary hole. The destination is lost, so the resolver offers the whole account list instead."}
{"id":"ft-account-only-no-category","bucket":"free_text","text":"1200 kotak","expect":{"outcome":"write","format":"free_text","candidate":{"amount":1200,"account_alias":"Kotak Credit Card"}},"expectedFailure":true,"baseline":{"outcome":"ask"},"note":"KNOWN GAP: trailingAlias() only scans AFTER a matched category keyword, so with no category word in the text a bare trailing account name is invisible. Limitation of the heuristic."}
